From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <openbmc@ctopai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: hid: classify cancelled IN requests

Disabling an endpoint completes pending HID IN requests with -ESHUTDOWN.
Dequeuing a request or resetting an endpoint can also cancel it. These are
expected lifecycle completions, as already handled by the HID OUT path,
and should not produce an error on the console.

Keep unexpected failures visible and always clear write_pending and wake
writers, including when the request was cancelled.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: CEB-GNRD maintainers <openbmc@ctopai.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
@@ -437,9 +437,19 @@ static void f_hidg_req_complete(struct usb_ep *ep, struct usb_request *req)
 	struct f_hidg *hidg = (struct f_hidg *)ep->driver_data;
 	unsigned long flags;
 
-	if (req->status != 0) {
+	switch (req->status) {
+	case 0:
+		break;
+	case -ECONNABORTED: /* hardware forced ep reset */
+	case -ECONNRESET:   /* request dequeued */
+	case -ESHUTDOWN:    /* disconnect from host */
+		VDBG(hidg->func.config->cdev,
+		     "HID IN request cancelled: %d\n", req->status);
+		break;
+	default:
 		ERROR(hidg->func.config->cdev,
 			"End Point Request ERROR: %d\n", req->status);
+		break;
 	}
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&hidg->write_spinlock, flags);
